  ("Neh 8","Ezra publicly reads and explains God's law to the assembled people, resulting in both weeping and joyful celebration."),
  ("Neh 9","The community observes an extended time of confession and worship, recounting Israel's history of God's faithfulness and their own repeated failures."),
